WEBVTT

00:08:30.204 --> 00:08:33.078
In fact, these are the key ingredients
that Martine has found

00:08:33.102 --> 00:08:34.965
for making remote teams effective.

00:08:35.698 --> 00:08:37.665
But how do you build them among teammates

00:08:37.689 --> 00:08:41.071
who can only see the dimly lit,
poorly framed video conference versions

00:08:41.095 --> 00:08:42.251
of each other?

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.416
Let's start with shared identity.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:48.366
It's the sense that
we're all in this together.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:50.749
When teams lose that sense of unity ...

00:08:50.773 --> 00:08:54.636
MH: ... it's really easy to get
an us-versus-them kind of dynamic going.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:58.946
"Here in Philadelphia,
we work really hard,

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.875
but that part of the team
that's over there in Belgium,